SPU: the overlay source table's size (SPU_OVL_SRC_MAX) may be defined at build time.

Resistance 3 lifts about 220 SPU images, 213 of them Insomniac job modules registered as resident regions (every
module of its job system; the buffer modules no census placed are lifted position-independent). The table of
overlay sources holds 128: past that spu_overlay_register_verified_region fails, and the last 88 modules registered stayed
in the interpreter. The default stays 128; the port defines a larger one from its own build, like SPU_WORKLOAD_MAX.

Test: a scripted boot to the Haven street fight, aiming: no "[r3] ... not registered" line in the log (88 without
the larger cap), and the interpreter census of that fight (see the commit) drops to the modules no lift covers.
The workflows build test_spu_lifted_start with -DSPU_OVL_SRC_MAX=512: with the regions the domain's earlier
patches and upstream's test_reloc_regions register, its last tests otherwise find the default table full.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

